+# Instructions append
+
+## Matcher interface
+
+`Matcher::new(matcher, subs)` takes the rule as a function that receives the element by value, `F: Fn(T) -> bool + 'static`, and the word to substitute as anything that can be viewed as a string, `S: AsRef<str>`.
+The tests build matchers from closures such as `|n: u32| n % 4 == 0`, so a matcher that expects a reference (`Fn(&T) -> bool`) does not compile against them.
+
